From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Propagate generator exceptions before completed-handle handling
License: MIT
Source: a-n-t-h-o-n-y/zzz commit 9d7c047f47c81a95a5ea824075253618356593a2
Source-file: include/zzz/coro.hpp SHA256 db3df750b5a860e93489db1beefdfc48fc091f8e934edc6ca19f6ccbdfd3fa34
Root-cause: stored coroutine exceptions are lost when completion becomes end
Applies-to: TermOx 2.0.0 bundled zzz exact commit 9d7c047f47c81a95a5ea824075253618356593a2
Upstream: not submitted
Remove-when: official dependency checks exceptions after both resume sites,
 and the complete strict target regressions pass without this patch

Keep the owning Generator and non-owning iterators unchanged. Check the
stored promise exception after both resume sites, before treating done
as end-of-range. Original archive notices are retained before this patch.

--- a/.packaging-deps/zzz/include/zzz/coro.hpp
+++ b/.packaging-deps/zzz/include/zzz/coro.hpp
@@ -102,2 +102,5 @@
                 handle_.resume();
+                if (handle_.promise().exception) {
+                    std::rethrow_exception(handle_.promise().exception);
+                }
                 if (handle_.done()) { handle_ = nullptr; }
@@ -110,6 +113,6 @@
                 handle_.resume();
-                if (handle_.done()) { handle_ = nullptr; }
-                else if (handle_.promise().exception) {
+                if (handle_.promise().exception) {
                     std::rethrow_exception(handle_.promise().exception);
                 }
+                if (handle_.done()) { handle_ = nullptr; }
             }
